---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '@/components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '@/data/site';

const lastUpdated = 'June 1, 2025';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="WealthHarbor's privacy policy explains how we collect, use, and protect your personal information."
  canonical="/privacy-policy"
>
  <div class="container-main py-8 lg:py-12 max-w-3xl">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[
      { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
      { label: 'Privacy Policy' },
    ]} />

    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-surface-900 mb-2">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-surface-800 mb-8">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <div class="prose-content space-y-8 text-surface-800">
      <section>
        <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
        <p>WealthHarbor ("we," "us," or "our") operates {siteConfig.url} (the "Site"). This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, disclose, and safeguard your information when you visit our website, subscribe to our newsletter, use our calculators, or contact us.</p>
        <p>By using the Site, you consent to the practices described in this policy. If you do not agree, please discontinue use of the Site.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
        <h3>2.1 Information You Provide</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Contact forms:</strong> Name, email address, subject, and message content when you contact us.</li>
          <li><strong>Newsletter:</strong> Email address when you subscribe to our mailing list.</li>
          <li><strong>Correspondence:</strong> Any information you include in emails or other communications with us.</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>2.2 Automatically Collected Information</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Log data:</strong> IP address, browser type, operating system, referring URLs, pages viewed, and timestamps.</li>
          <li><strong>Cookies and similar technologies:</strong> See our <a href="/cookie-policy">Cookie Policy</a> for details.</li>
          <li><strong>Analytics data:</strong> Aggregated usage statistics via third-party analytics services.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>3. How We Use Your Information</h2>
        <p>We use collected information to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Respond to inquiries and provide customer support</li>
          <li>Send newsletters and educational content you have opted into</li>
          <li>Improve our website, content, and user experience</li>
          <li>Analyze traffic patterns and measure content performance</li>
          <li>Detect and prevent fraud, spam, and abuse</li>
          <li>Comply with legal obligations</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We do not sell your personal information to third parties.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>4. Legal Basis for Processing (EEA/UK Users)</h2>
        <p>If you are located in the European Economic Area or United Kingdom, we process your data based on:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Consent:</strong> Newsletter subscriptions and non-essential cookies</li>
          <li><strong>Legitimate interests:</strong> Site security, analytics, and content improvement</li>
          <li><strong>Contractual necessity:</strong> Responding to contact form submissions</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>5. Third-Party Services</h2>
        <p>We may share information with trusted service providers who assist us in operating the Site:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Email marketing:</strong> Newsletter delivery platforms (e.g., Mailchimp, ConvertKit)</li>
          <li><strong>Analytics:</strong> Google Analytics or similar services for aggregated traffic analysis</li>
          <li><strong>Advertising:</strong> Google AdSense and related ad networks, if approved and enabled in the future (see <a href="/advertising-disclosure">Advertising Disclosure</a>)</li>
          <li><strong>Hosting:</strong> Web hosting providers for Site infrastructure</li>
        </ul>
        <p>These providers are contractually obligated to protect your data and use it only for the services they provide to us.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>6. Cookies</h2>
        <p>We use cookies and similar tracking technologies. You can manage cookie preferences through your browser settings. For full details, see our <a href="/cookie-policy">Cookie Policy</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>7. Data Retention</h2>
        <p>We retain personal information only as long as necessary for the purposes described in this policy:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Newsletter subscriptions: Until you unsubscribe</li>
          <li>Contact form submissions: Up to 24 months</li>
          <li>Analytics data: As configured by our analytics provider (typically 14–26 months)</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>8. Your Rights</h2>
        <p>Depending on your location, you may have the right to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Access the personal data we hold about you</li>
          <li>Request correction of inaccurate data</li>
          <li>Request deletion of your data</li>
          <li>Object to or restrict certain processing</li>
          <li>Withdraw consent at any time (without affecting prior processing)</li>
          <li>Data portability</li>
          <li>Lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority</li>
        </ul>
        <p>To exercise these rights, contact us at <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.email}`}>{siteConfig.email}</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>9. California Privacy Rights (CCPA/CPRA)</h2>
        <p>California residents have additional rights under the California Consumer Privacy Act, including the right to know what personal information is collected, request deletion, and opt out of the sale or sharing of personal information. We do not sell personal information. To submit a request, email {siteConfig.email} with the subject line "California Privacy Request."</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>10. Children's Privacy</h2>
        <p>The Site is not directed to children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe a child has provided us with personal data, contact us and we will promptly delete it.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>11. Security</h2>
        <p>We implement reasonable technical and organizational measures to protect your information, including HTTPS encryption, access controls, and secure hosting. However, no method of transmission over the Internet is 100% secure.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>12. International Transfers</h2>
        <p>Your information may be processed in countries other than your own. We ensure appropriate safeguards are in place for international data transfers, including standard contractual clauses where required.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>13. Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>We may update this Privacy Policy periodically. Changes will be posted on this page with an updated "Last updated" date. Material changes will be communicated via email to newsletter subscribers where appropriate.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>14. Contact Us</h2>
        <p>Questions about this Privacy Policy? Contact us at <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.email}`}>{siteConfig.email}</a> or visit our <a href="/contact">Contact page</a>.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
